e player has more tools  they can go invisible they can fetch  things there were so many more choices  we wanted to allow the player to take a  second take a breath and think about  what they want to do because it this is  the deepest gameplay that a Gears game  has ever had and so we wanted the player  to have the chance to think about it a  number of battles you'll go into the  space and you'll actually get to see the  swarm kind of just mingling about  because they don't know you're there yet  and that was a big change for us and and  part of that stealthy ability to cloak  and go all the way upstairs and take out  the sniper first it was part of that as  well let's look at a couple of the  abilities we ended up not using this  idea of dropping cover we wanted to  create this sort of idea of a temporary  force field if you will and we shouldn't  even played with the idea that it was  movable that you could actually lean  into it and start pushing it around as  you can see here it's  got really complicated and we use it a  little bit on the ice and so you know we  had we took that prototype and we  leveraged it in the level a few places  where you could push ice on ice kind of  things it just made the level design so  challenging to know that jacket would  cover anywhere that anytime you were  trying to make a challenge for the  player Jack had sort of override it  immediately by just allowing to drop  cover so it was just too game-changing  for us and that's why we got rid of it  we also went with like this idea that  you know Jack could be a fabricator you  know the sort of 3d printer in our world  we tried prototypes of Jack having the  ability of dropping turrets you could  get onto we had Jack drop decoys to  attract enemies to it but again instead  of being sort of the support where you  felt like it was helping you shoot and  it was kind of helping you in the  moment-to-moment gameplay it felt sort  of a fundamental difference and it also  made it sort of c