o because  otherwise like you can expect Jack to  start the next thing with all of these  abilities you've upgraded and everything  and this allows us to kind of get rid of  that and so if we were to bring Jack  forward then you could have a fresh Jack  and start all over again  right so it's one of those things where  it's kind of like good for the story I'm  good for the design basically what we  wanted to as we were saying how do we  get to this point where we can have Jack  make his own decision and this was gonna  be a big moment as basically you're  fighting this giant monster you're going  to use these rail guns and you're gonna  learn pretty quickly like we can kind of  piss it off we can hurt it but we're not  going to win and so this entire game  you've been giving jack orders go do  that go do this open that door  give me that ammo cover me in clove  could give me some health so we wanted  this moment where Jack makes a decision  and Jack shuts down Baird and he decides  nope I'm gonna save the day I have the  beacon coordinates I can do this Jack  heroically sacrifices himself to save  the squad and the city and humanity and  so you have this really interesting  moment of this character that you've  been investing in throughout the entire  game and grown attached to and he does a  heroic sacrifice to save everybody else  and the number of people who have told  us and reacted to the fact that this  piece of metal with teardrop-shaped eyes  caused them to get teary eyed and  emotional and upset and yell at us and  swear at us because we killed someone  they truly liked liked and enjoyed  having their squad I meant a lot to us  and I felt like we accomplished our  goals with that so I mean when you look  at the journey now tears came out of  2006 so it's been 13 and a half years  like we go from this lock-and-key robot  that didn't really mean that much to  this squad other than baird and now  we've taken him 13 years later to this  place where he's a meaningful character  to the players who played either asked  him or with him and it was really  interesting to have that that journey to  go from this simple device to now this  sort of almost fully fleshed out  character that had abilities and meaning  and gameplay and in its own story arc  and on the journey and so when he looks  at you in the scene with his sad eyes  knowing he's going to have to make this  choice that Jack is choosing to destroy  himself in order to save everybody else  and so it was kind of a pivotal moment  and it helped us feel like a great sort  of arc of where Jack had started from to  where now Jack is ending and it meant a  lot to us he's a meaningful character  and everybody knows Jack when you think  about the squad in Marcus Tom and on  and Cole and Baird like Jack's part of  that and this felt like a really big  cherry on top of the sundae just you  know to sort of honor Jack as a  character in our game when I think about  when people come together they come for  the story we're given permission because  of the world we've built to have this  comic book sort of sensibilities we can  laugh at ourselves we can make really  bad jokes and and sort of have dark  humor we can have this sort of  blockbuster action movie sequences and  over-the-top set pieces and it's like a  summer blockbuster and then we can have  these sort of sweet moments sort of  sadness where whether it's the Morea  scene or the Dom scene or you know the  choice or or Jack the fact that we can  go from this sort of big men with thick  necks and all that stuff and we're able  to go now to where we're at a place and  play with that and make our storytelling  more contemporary and deal with grays  instead of black and whites where we can  have more complex characters and more  nuanced characters and yet we can still  bring out the emotion and and the fact  that people are responding that way to  the to the story is just so meaningful  to all of us and and we couldn't have  done it without you know obviously the  technical talents to be able to show  this stuff on screen but the voices the  cast that we have is amazing and Tom  Bissell's writing is amazing and it's  just been an amazing collaboration to be  able to tell this story and do it the  way we did  [Music]  you
 

